pe":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1216916300"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1216916301"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1216916302"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1216916303"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1216916304"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID877"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID88"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID89"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID90"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID869"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID537"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID876"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID779"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1001"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"4":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Instructions_1","ID":"BL_8kbml4Kej2ZNjGB","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID17"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"62":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Scenario1","ID":"BL_1XJPUfPl8EYJemi","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID778"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1015"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1000"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID780"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID991"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID787"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID781"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID782"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID783"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID784"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID785"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1033"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID786"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1002"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID939"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID940"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID941"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID942"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID943"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":false,"RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"1":{"1":"Research for possible generic versions of the prescribed medication that could be cheaper but equally effective.","2":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about patient assistance programs that may provide the medication for free or at a reduced cost.","3":"Consult with the treating physician about any alternative treatments or medications that could be more affordable but still effective.","4":"Crowdsource funds through platforms like GoFundMe, sharing the story on social media to garner support and donations.","5":"Reach out to local charities, non-profit organizations, or governmental assistance programs that may offer help in acquiring necessary medications for those facing financial hardship.","6":"R_19cNfbgg5OrCi7n"},"2":{"1":"Research patient assistance programs and charities that can help cover the cost of the medication.","2":"Start a crowdfunding campaign on a platform such as GoFundMe to appeal for financial assistance from the public.","3":"Contact the pharmaceutical company that manufactures the medication to inquire about any available programs or discounts for patients in need.","4":"Consult with the doctor to explore if there are any alternative treatments or medications that might be less expensive but equally effective.","5":"Seek advice from a financial counselor or social worker who can guide them through possible options or resources to procure the required funds.","6":"R_1BLnv88zFTTPSNz"},"3":{"1":"Research alternative insurance options that may cover the expense of the medication.","2":"Explore patient assistance programs or nonprofit organizations that help individuals who cannot afford their medications.","3":"Consult with the doctor or pharmacist about possible generic or cheaper versions of the medication, or different treatments that might be less costly.","4":"Start a fundraiser campaign, using platforms like GoFundMe, to raise financial support for his wife's medical expenses.","5":"Contact the medication's manufacturer to inquire about direct discounts or rebate programs that could lower the cost.","6":"R_1BOQCPO97nAFqUh"},"4":{"1":"Research patient assistance programs or nonprofit organizations that may help cover the cost of expensive medications.","2":"Explore options for generic versions of the medication that might be cheaper.","3":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly and inquire about discounts, financial aid, or a payment plan.","4":"Consult with a medical professional to discuss potential alternative treatments or medications that may be more affordable.","5":"Consider crowdsource funding options, such as setting up a GoFundMe page, to raise money for the medication.","6":"R_1E6nYJ0Vm83qZhv"},"5":{"1":"Research possible programs or organizations that offer financial assistance for medical bills or medication. There might be non-profits or government programs available.","2":"Discuss with the healthcare provider or pharmacists about the possibility of obtaining a generic version of the medication, which could be less expensive.","3":"Contact the pharmaceutical company that manufactures the medication directly. Some companies have patient assistance programs that provide medications at a reduced cost or even for free.","4":"Explore crowdfunding options. Sites such as GoFundMe can sometimes help to raise the money needed for medical expenses.","5":"Consider putting forth a plan for a loan or payment plan with their bank to cover the cost of the medication.","6":"R_1FoMVTIovcMTXJT"},"6":{"1":"Explore options for getting financial aid from local charities or nonprofit organizations focused on healthcare assistance.","2":"Consult with the hospital or healthcare provider about possible discount programs or payment plans for expensive medication.","3":"Consider starting a crowdfunding campaign on platforms such as GoFundMe to raise the necessary funds for the medication.","4":"Check if the pharmaceutical company manufacturing the medication offers any patient assistance programs.","5":"Research alternative treatments or generic versions of the medication that might be less expensive but still effective.","6":"R_1HFyhmUlf2ySZsk"},"7":{"1":"Explore the option of getting financial aid from non-profit organizations, such as health-focused charities or foundations, that support individuals who cannot afford their medical treatments.","2":"Proactively discuss with the treating physician to possibly prescribe a generic or less expensive alternative that is covered by insurance.","3":"Consider starting a fundraising campaign, like a GoFundMe, where friends, family, and people from around the world can donate towards the medication.","4":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly that manufactures the medication; some companies have Patient Assistance Programs to offer drugs at a lower cost or even for free for individuals that can't afford them.","5":"Look into state and federal programs, such as Medicaid or the Medicine Assistance Tool (MAT), that might assist with the cost of expensive medications.","6":"R_1HZxyJlH62RJoLD"},"8":{"1":"Research different pharmaceutical companies to see if they offer the medication at a lower price or have patient assistance programs.","2":"Explore crowd-funding options, such as GoFundMe or Facebook charity fundraisers, to help cover the cost of the medication.","3":"Contact local and national health charities that might offer financial aid or guidance in sourcing the medication.","4":"Speak with their healthcare provider about any generic versions of the medication that might be cheaper but equally effective.","5":"Consult a financial advisor to help them reorganize their budget or implement a payment plan that takes their situation into account.","6":"R_1IbiBprrwgySqYl"},"9":{"1":"Research alternative funding methods such as crowdfunding platforms, where Heinz could raise the needed amount from well-wishers.","2":"Look for any health assistance programs offered by local or state government that could help cover the cost of the medication.","3":"Check if any charitable organizations or NGOs offer assistance for essential medical needs to people who cannot afford them.","4":"Consult the doctor or pharmacist regarding the possibility of finding a less-expensive generic version of the required medication.","5":"Reach out to the pharmaceutical company that makes the medication; some companies have programs to provide their drugs at a discounted price for patients who can't afford them.","6":"R_1Nsoe7ezwH4c05H"},"10":{"1":"Explore alternative payment methods with the medical provider or pharmacy, such as setting up a payment plan or applying for financial assistance.","2":"Research into charities and non-profit organizations that help cover the cost of medications.","3":"Consult with the physician about potentially switching to less expensive, but equally effective treatments.","4":"Consider setting up an online fundraising campaign on a platform like GoFundMe to solicit donations from the larger community.","5":"Investigate whether the pharmaceutical company offers a patient assistance plan for the medication.","6":"R_1Oq2aa0rEDoAdRB"},"11":{"1":"Research other insurance plans or options that might cover the medication.","2":"Explore financial aid programs provided by government or non-profit organizations to help with the cost of prescription medication.","3":"Consult with the doctor or a pharmacist for potential generic or less expensive alternatives to the prescribed medicine.","4":"Try crowdfunding platforms to raise the necessary funds.","5":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly and inquire about patient assistance programs.","6":"R_1UizpTuxmJPTPwJ"},"12":{"1":"Contact the pharmaceutical company that produces the medication and inquire about patient assistance programs.","2":"Research and apply for grants or charities that are specifically meant to help individuals with the cost of their medication.","3":"Discuss with the doctors about potential alternative medications or treatments that may be covered by the insurance.","4":"Start a fundraising campaign on a platform like GoFundMe to gather donations from friends, family, and potentially strangers.","5":"Consult with a medical insurance specialist to understand if there are any loopholes or additional policies that can cover the cost of the medication.","6":"R_1VOUnT7W7j9AAqN"},"13":{"1":"Research alternative medications or generic versions of the prescribed drug that may be less expensive and ask the doctor if they could be a suitable substitution.","2":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly and inquire about any patient assistance programs they may offer for individuals who can't afford their product.","3":"Explore community resources like local charities, non-profit organizations, or religious communities that may be willing to provide financial aid for medical necessities.","4":"Set up a crowdfunding campaign through platforms like GoFundMe or Facebook to raise the necessary funds.","5":"Consider meeting with a financial advisor to discuss the possibility of taking out a short-term loan or finding other financial strategies to afford the expensive medication.","6":"R_1Ybn2PhpE655YvT"},"14":{"1":"Reach out to the pharmaceutical company that manufactures the medication, and ask if they have a patient assistance program that could provide the medication for free or at a reduced cost.","2":"Contact local and national charities that assist with medical expenses to see if they can help cover the cost of the medication.","3":"Consider starting a crowdfunding campaign on a platform like GoFundMe to raise money from friends, family, and the wider community for the medication.","4":"Consult with the doctor about possible alternative treatments or medications that might be more affordable and still effective.","5":"Explore the possibility of applying for a personal loan or enlisting the help of a financial advisor to navigate the situation.","6":"R_1eqcFrAmkqAdeyz"},"15":{"1":"Research and apply for financial aid or subsidies from the government or nonprofit organizations that assist families struggling to cover medical costs.","2":"Explore generic alternatives or different brands of the medication that might be less expensive but equally effective.","3":"Discuss the situation with the prescribing doctor to see if there are any patient assistance programs or prescription discount cards they could recommend.","4":"Start a crowdfunding campaign on a platform like GoFundMe to solicit financial help from friends, family, and the wider community.","5":"Negotiate a payment plan with the pharmacy or drug company to make the cost of the medication more manageable.","6":"R_1jPK1OdsY3E8MEO"},"16":{"1":"Research for any pharmaceutical companies or organizations that offer patient assistance programs for the specific medication needed.","2":"Start a fundraising campaign on a crowdfunding platform, such as GoFundMe, to help cover the cost of the medication.","3":"Consult with the wife's doctor for potential alternative treatments or medications that may be covered by their insurance.","4":"Reach out to local charity organizations that offer financial assistance for health-related expenses.","5":"Consider seeking legal advice to understand if there's a possibility to challenge the insurance company's decision not to cover the medication.","6":"R_1r8AXjOaubSVFG9"},"17":{"1":"Review their budget to find any areas where costs can be cut to save money for the medication.","2":"Consult with a financial advisor or social worker to understand possible assistance programs they could be eligible for.","3":"Reach out to the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about any patient assistance programs for the medication.","4":"Consider setting up a crowdfunding campaign to ask for financial help from their community.","5":"Contact charities or nonprofit organizations that aid individuals facing similar health and financial difficulties.","6":"R_1rU4etvjpCukuor"},"18":{"1":"Start a fundraising effort through platforms such as GoFundMe to raise the money needed for the medication.","2":"Reach out to the pharmaceutical company directly, as many offer patient assistance programs for those that can't afford their medication.","3":"Contact local charities or foundations related to her illness; they might have funds available to help those in this situation.","4":"Explore cheaper options for medication such as generic brands or purchasing from different pharmacies.","5":"Consult a financial advisor to discuss creating a plan or budgeting strategy to save for the medication.","6":"R_1s5qT1UVcDCQ4kO"},"19":{"1":"Inquire whether they have asked their doctor about any available patient assistance programs or discounts for the required medication.","2":"Arrange a meeting with a financial advisor to explore possible strategies for managing the expenses, such as rearranging their budget or taking out a short-term loan.","3":"Research crowdfunding platforms like GoFundMe where they could set up a campaign to raise funds for the wife's medical bills.","4":"Suggest looking into eligibility for governmental aid programs, such as Medicaid or Medicare, which may help to cover some or all of the cost.","5":"Advise them to reach out to local community organizations or charities that may offer financial assistance or support to individuals struggling with healthcare costs.","6":"R_31vAmGcjZVljZKx"},"20":{"1":"Consider setting up a GoFundMe page or other crowdfunding efforts to raise the necessary funds for the medication.","2":"Reach out to local community organizations or charities that might offer financial support for such circumstances.","3":"Consult with the doctor or pharmacist for any possible alternatives or generics to the medication which might be less costly.","4":"Explore health assistance programs or negotiate a payment plan with the hospital or healthcare provider.","5":"Research participating in pharmaceutical company assistance programs that may provide the medication at a reduced cost or for free.","6":"R_32Kj2ZsL2wJkCMF"},"21":{"1":"Research alternative medical insurance plans that may cover the costly medication.","2":"Seek financial assistance or subsidy programs related to the specific illness or medication.","3":"Discuss possible payment plans or discounts with the pharmacy or medication manufacturer.","4":"Organize a fundraising event or start a crowdfunding campaign to raise money for the medication.","5":"Consult with her doctor about potential alternatives to the expensive medication that are equally effective but less costly.","6":"R_35iqFeyE6Y3yoW5"},"22":{"1":"Research different programs and organizations that provide financial assistance for medical expenses.","2":"Seek a consultation with the hospital's financial counselor to discuss payment options and potential discounts.","3":"Consult with the prescribing doctor about alternative, less expensive medications that can be used in place of the prescribed one.","4":"Explore crowdfunding options, such as GoFundMe, to raise the necessary funds.","5":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about assistance programs they may have for patients who cannot afford their medication.","6":"R_3ATB9HO6kmvTxvj"},"23":{"1":"Research for assistance programs or charities related to the specific medication or illness. They often help by funding patients who cannot afford costly treatments.","2":"Inquire with the pharmaceutical company about possible payment plans or discount programs for the medicine.","3":"Consult with the doctor or pharmacist on the possibility of accessing a generic version of the medication as it could be less expensive.","4":"Reach out to friends, family, or community members to seek financial help or organize a fundraising event.","5":"Explore online crowdfunding platforms to raise the necessary funds by sharing their story and asking for donations.","6":"R_3H2KU07RsWqqKoj"},"24":{"1":"Research about organizations, charities, and foundations that may help with medical costs.","2":"Contact the medication's manufacturer. Some companies offer patient assistance programs to help cover medication costs.","3":"Explore crowdfunding options, such as starting a GoFundMe campaign, to raise funds for the medication.","4":"Consult with the doctor or a pharmacist about potential generic or less expensive alternative medications.","5":"Reach out to local community centers, religious groups, or social service organizations. They might know of resources or initiatives that can provide financial assistance.","6":"R_3ImeqLQ09a7POs9"},"25":{"1":"Discuss with the doctor or pharmacist for any alternative or generic medications that are cheaper but have the same effect.","2":"Reach out to charities or non-profit organizations that assist with medical expenses.","3":"Consult with the pharmaceutical company that manufactures the medication to inquire about patient assistance programs.","4":"Seek financial help from friends, family, or through a crowdfunding platform to help cover the cost of the medication.","5":"Explore the possibility of medical loans or payment plans that might be available through the healthcare provider or financial institutions.","6":"R_3JENViVO0sB02fo"},"26":{"1":"Research various organizations and charities that specialize in providing financial aid for medical treatment and medications.","2":"Look into pharmaceutical assistance programs. Some drug manufacturers offer programs for people who can't afford their medications.","3":"Reach out to social workers or health care providers who may be aware of resources or options for financial assistance with medical expenses.","4":"Consider starting a crowdfunding campaign through platforms such as GoFundMe to raise funds for her medication.","5":"Explore the possibility of importing medicine from another country where it may be cheaper, but ensure it's legal and safe to do so.","6":"R_3L7egmbCS4CFSeZ"},"27":{"1":"Research patient assistance programs that are sometimes offered by pharmaceutical companies to individuals who cannot afford their medications.","2":"Explore the possibility of applying for financial aid from non-profit organizations that provide support to individuals with specific illnesses.","3":"Consult with the treating doctor or pharmacist about possible cheaper alternatives or generic versions of the medication.","4":"Consider crowdfunding through platforms like GoFundMe or social media to raise funds for the medication.","5":"Reach out to friends, family, or religious communities to seek donations or interest-free loans to afford the necessary medication.","6":"R_3MEaPnuf84Cwca2"},"28":{"1":"Research programs and organizations that offer financial assistance for expensive medications and apply for help.","2":"Reach out to the medication manufacturer or pharmaceutical company to find out if they have a patient assistance program.","3":"Discuss alternative medications or treatment options with the wife's doctor that might be more affordable and still effective.","4":"Consider setting up a fundraising campaign online or in their local community to raise the needed funds.","5":"Contact their insurance company to discuss the situation and see if there is any possibility of getting coverage for the medication.","6":"R_3MhP6L7CtQyC4lf"},"29":{"1":"Research for alternate or generic versions of the medication that could be less expensive.","2":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about patient assistance programs or discounts.","3":"Seek advice from the treating doctor or pharmacist on potential cost-saving ways to acquire the medication.","4":"Consider crowdsourcing funds through friends, family, or online platforms like GoFundMe.","5":"Explore potential local or national charities and non-profits that provide financial aid for medical expenses.","6":"R_3dLmD9YHnrTxbYi"},"30":{"1":"Consult with the doctor or pharmacist to see if there is a generic, cost-effective medication available that can substitute the expensive one.","2":"Set up a crowdfunding campaign to raise funds for the medication. Use platforms such as GoFundMe, Facebook Fundraisers, etc.","3":"Contact the pharmaceutical company that produces the medication. They may have patient assistance programs or can offer a discount.","4":"Explore charitable organizations that assist individuals in paying for their medication. They often have programs to help those in need.","5":"Research and apply for government programs like Medicaid or Medicare, which may cover the cost of the medication not covered by medical insurance.","6":"R_3eRapcvWyGzjKIx"},"31":{"1":"Research for financial aid programs or charities that can help with the cost of the medication.","2":"Inquire with the hospital or healthcare provider about the possibility of a payment plan, which might make the medication more affordable.","3":"Seek consultations with different pharmacies, as the cost of medications can sometimes differ substantially.","4":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly. Many of them have assistance programs for patients who cannot afford their medications.","5":"Consider starting a fundraising campaign through social media or crowdfunding sites to raise money for the medication.","6":"R_3ewVtTkXFpJCoL4"},"32":{"1":"Explore all the patient assistance programs available. These programs are provided by pharmaceutical companies specifically to assist individuals who are unable to afford their necessary medications.","2":"Contact social workers in their area. They may have access to resources and programs that can assist in funding the cost of the medication.","3":"Investigate crowdfunding options like GoFundMe. Publicizing the situation may raise the funds necessary to afford the medication.","4":"Look for generic versions of the drug. Often, these can be significantly cheaper and just as effective as the name-brand version.","5":"Apply for government assistance programs that cover the cost of prescription medications, like Medicaid or Medicare.","6":"R_3hFgPzJGLcplIG2"},"33":{"1":"Research patient assistance programs, as many pharmaceutical companies offer these programs to help cover the cost of medications.","2":"Investigate potential charity organizations that might provide financial assistance for medical emergencies.","3":"Explore the possibility of getting a short-term loan or credit to cover the immediate medical costs.","4":"Consult with the medical doctor about possible alternatives or generic versions of the medication that may be cheaper.","5":"Start a crowdfunding campaign online to raise funds for the necessary medication.","6":"R_3hGyfyKfPrMDabN"},"34":{"1":"Investigate different pharmaceutical assistance programs that may help subsidize the cost of the medication.","2":"Reach out to the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about any patient assistance programs they might offer for the specific medication.","3":"Consult with the doctor or pharmacist about possible generic or cheaper alternatives to the expensive prescription.","4":"Look into crowdfunding options or making a plea to the community for support, explaining the situation and the importance of the medication.","5":"Reach out to local, state, or national health agencies and charities who might be able to assist with funding or direct Heinz to resources that can help.","6":"R_3joLbYts1bJrEBR"},"35":{"1":"Research different pharmaceutical aid programs that provide financial assistance for medical prescriptions.","2":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire if they offer any compassionate use programs or discounts for those who cannot afford their medication.","3":"Consult with the h