dition.","6":"R_5RfVrMBM84WXsEF"},"58":{"1":"Start a fundraising campaign on a crowdfunding platform such as GoFundMe, detailing the situation and the exact cost of the medication.","2":"Reach out to pharmaceutical companies or foundations that offer patient assistance programs, to see if they can get the medication at a discounted rate or for free.","3":"Seek advice from their doctor or pharmacist about any possible subsidies, or if there are effective, less expensive alternatives to the medication.","4":"Explore working part-time or freelance to supplement their income, or sell unneeded items for quick cash.","5":"Consider contacting local charities and nonprofits that could possibly assist with the financial burden associated with the medication costs.","6":"R_5YtgHCY0j6X8jZ8"},"59":{"1":"Research for charities or organizations that offer financial support for medical bills. These often exist for those who can't afford critical medication.","2":"Consult with the prescribing doctor regarding possible alternatives or generic versions of the medication that might equally effective but less costly.","3":"Inspect the possibility of setting up an online crowdfunding campaign to raise the much-needed funds for the medication.","4":"Communicate with the pharmaceutical company that manufactures the medication. They may have programs that help with the cost or can provide the medication at a discounted rate.","5":"Consider enlisting the help of a lawyer or patient advocate. They might assist in appealing to the insurance company to get the medication covered.","6":"R_5eRBvP0sxZai36F"},"60":{"1":"Explore alternative insurance options or plans that might cover the cost of the medication.","2":"Contact the pharmaceutical company directly to inquire about any compassionate use programs, discounts, or payment plans they may offer.","3":"Research fundraising possibilities such as starting a GoFundMe page or hosting local community fundraising to help cover the costs.","4":"Consu