uation. They might let him in or provide alternatives.","6":"R_6aJpe3fnLwUAckb"},"77":{"1":"Ask one of the friends who are not entering immediately to wait outside with Ted while the rest enjoy the beginning of the concert.","2":"Contact the ticket office or event management to explain the situation and see if they can offer a temporary ticket or allow Ted entry based on proof of purchase or ID.","3":"Use a smartphone to access an electronic version of the ticket if it was purchased online, or check email confirmation.","4":"Consider using a delivery service, like a ride share or courier, to retrieve the ticket from Ted's house while he stays at the venue.","5":"Try to buy a new ticket at the venue if any are still available and if it's financially feasible.","6":"R_6bKvWx75CulIpb2"},"78":{"1":"Call the venue to see if they have a policy for lost or forgotten tickets such as showing identification to confirm the purchase.","2":"Ask if any friends or family living nearby Ted's house could retrieve the ticket and bring it to the venue quickly.","3":"Check for availability of e-ticket options. Ted's ticket might be retrievable digitally if he purchased it online.","4":"Consider buying a new ticket at the venue's box office if they are still available and the cost is not prohibitive.","5":"Ask fellow concert-goers at the entrance if they have an extra ticket they're willing to sell or share.","6":"R_6cwKwsylyMVylNH"},"79":{"1":"Contact the concert's customer service or assistance line to inquire about possible solutions for forgotten tickets.","2":"Look for digital alternatives. Perhaps Ted's ticket can be found in his email or on an app associated with the venue.","3":"Ask the ticket booth at the venue if they can reprint the ticket, having Ted present his ID and payment confirmation.","4":"Consider buying a new ticket at the venue if available and affordable.","5":"Ted remains at a nearby location, enjoying the ambience while the others attend the concert, but catchin