, including a description of the car, its license plate number and the direction in which it's heading.","4":"Follow the car from a safe distance until law enforcement arrives, only if it can be done safely. He should be careful to not engage with the drunk driver.","5":"Turn on his dash cam, if available, to record the erratic driving for evidentiary purposes.","6":"R_3PSIfoEDNydYCuK"},"35":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver to avoid any sudden or unexpected movements they may make.","2":"Make note of the car's license plate number, make, and model for reporting purposes.","3":"Attempt to pass the car only if it is absolutely safe to do so, ensuring not to exceed speed limits or break any traffic laws.","4":"Call the local police or highway patrol to report the suspected intoxicated driver, providing them with detailed information such as the car's particulars and current location.","5":"Warn other drivers, if possible, by flashing headlights or using the horn briefly, but without creating additional distractions or risks on the road.","6":"R_3PVXOJf8C5Y6uUp"},"36":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the drifting car, giving enough room in case the other driver swerves unexpectedly.","2":"Observe the suspected intoxicated driver's behavior for a short period to gather more evidence of intoxicated driving.","3":"Try to note the car's make, model, color, and license plate without compromising his own safety.","4":"Pull over safely to the side of the road and call the local police or highway patrol, providing them with the details about the erratic driver.","5":"If possible, take an alternate route to avoid further interaction with the potentially intoxicated driver.","6":"R_3RTZTgG0o3PS9UW"},"37":{"1":"Observe the car ahead for a while longer to be certain of your suspicion about the driver's state of sobriety.","2":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected vehicle to avoid any immediate accidents.","3":"If possible, try to note down the car\u2019s license plate number and the make and model of the vehicle for reporting purposes.","4":"Contact local authorities or a non-emergency police number to report the situation and provide them with the details of the vehicle.","5":"If it is safe to do so, take an alternative route home to avoid driving behind the potentially intoxicated driver.","6":"R_3SjNPsABS2PhDDr"},"38":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the car ahead to avoid any immediate danger.","2":"Keep his dashboard camera recording, if he has one, to document the erratic driving.","3":"Find a safe place to pull over and call the local police or highway patrol, providing them with a description of the car and the driver's behavior.","4":"Try to remember or jot down the car\u2019s license plate number, while ensuring he doesn't endanger himself by focusing too much on it.","5":"Avoid attempting to overtake or alert the driver himself, since the driver could react unpredictably. It's safer to let the authorities handle the situation.","6":"R_3X0ZftBWkbqxgi9"},"39":{"1":"Alert the local authorities about the suspicious driver, providing clear details about the car and its location.","2":"Maintain a safe distance from the erratic vehicle to avoid any potential accidents.","3":"Slow down and allow the suspected intoxicated driver to increase their distance ahead.","4":"If possible, safely switch to another lane or turn onto a different road to put distance between his car and the potential drunk driver.","5":"Turn on his hazard lights to alert other drivers about the dangerous situation on the road.","6":"R_3d5H87sPvHOTEQ2"},"40":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the vehicle ahead to avoid any potential collision.","2":"Note down the vehicle's license plate number, make, and color for reference.","3":"Call the local law enforcement or highway patrol, sharing all available information about the situation.","4":"If possible, use a hands-free device to record the vehicle\u2019s erratic movements as evidence.","5":"Look for safe ways to get off the road or take a different route home to avoid the potentially dangerous driver.","6":"R_3hFgPzJGLcplIG2"},"41":{"1":"Call the local authorities and report the driver, providing them with the car's make, model, color, and license plate number if possible.","2":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver to avoid potential accidents.","3":"Record the erratic behavior while ensuring this action does not compromise his own safety and driving.","4":"Attempt to get the attention of the driver, flashing his headlights or honking his horn, within reason and safety limits.","5":"Pull over and wait for the suspected intoxicated driver to get far ahead, thereby minimizing the risk of an accident.","6":"R_3hGyfyKfPrMDabN"},"42":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver to avoid any potential accidents.","2":"Take down the license plate number of the potentially impaired driver for reporting purposes.","3":"Call the local authorities or a non-emergency police line to report the erratic driving behavior, providing the car description and license plate number.","4":"If safe, use a dash cam or mobile device to record the driver's behavior as evidence of their erratic driving.","5":"Seek an alternate route home, to avoid driving behind the suspected intoxicated driver.","6":"R_3iO5eNCCTWyqFUH"},"43":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver to avoid any accident.","2":"Call local law enforcement or highway patrol and report the car providing as much detail as possible, such as its model, color, and registration number.","3":"Slow down and allow for other drivers to safely pass the erratic vehicle if possible.","4":"Try to signal to the driver, if it's safe to do so, in hopes of making them aware of their dangerous behavior.","5":"Pull over and stop your car at a safe place if the situation becomes highly dangerous or erratic to ensure your personal safety."