 crossing into the other lane.","3":"Avoid overtaking the vehicle, given the uncertainty of the driver's state and their unpredictable driving behavior.","4":"Contact local law enforcement to report the license plate number and dangerous driver to prevent potential accidents.","5":"Ensure his own safety and those around him by driving cautiously and staying alert to changes in the environment caused by the intoxicated driver.","6":"R_3t5vNRvNAcTavFF"},"48":{"1":"Slow down to maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver.","2":"Alert the local authorities with detailed information about the car and its behavior, including the license plate number if possible.","3":"Pull over to a safe place until the driver is further ahead or the authorities intervene.","4":"If possible, take an alternative route to avoid being on the same road as the suspected intoxicated driver.","5":"Try to alert other drivers around by honking the horn or flashing headlights to draw attention to the erratic behavior, but only as long as it is safe and will not increase the risk of an accident.","6":"R_3yncUFnsqUeiG0p"},"49":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the potentially intoxicated driver to avoid sudden erratic moves.","2":"Use the hands-free calling feature to dial the local police station, reporting the possible drunk driver and their license plate number.","3":"Avoid trying to pass the vehicle, as this could lead to an accident if the other driver suddenly swerves.","4":"Turn on hazard lights to warn other drivers of the potential danger ahead.","5":"Attempt to capture the erratic driving on a dashcam or cell phone camera (if a passenger is present) to provide evidence to law enforcement.","6":"R_40q414gjeTweXES"},"50":{"1":"Maintain a safe distance from the suspected intoxicated driver to avoid any sudden collisions.","2":"Record the number plate of the car, the make and model, color, and any other distinguishing features.","3":"Call the local police or highway patrol 