rives.","2":"If possible, lock up the store temporarily with a sign explaining the situation, and leave a note for his boss explaining his urgent situation.","3":"Get in touch with a local security firm or neighborhood watch who may be able to keep an eye on the store in his absence.","4":"Contact the police to inform them about the situation and see if they can send an officer to keep an eye on the store until the owner arrives.","5":"As a last resort, if he has enough time before the appointment, Jeff could wait for the first customers to arrive and explain the situation to them. He might find someone trustworthy who could hold the fort for a short while until his boss arrives.","6":"R_5nWiYkT7lRMPKyl"},"59":{"1":"Start calling his colleagues to check if any of them can cover up for him.","2":"If he has the contact of any family members or friends of the store owner, reach out to them and explain the situation.","3":"Consider closing the store temporarily, leaving a sign explaining the situation and the estimated reopening time.","4":"Report the situation to the authorities or the local police station if he has to leave but cannot close the store securely.","5":"Attempt to arrange a delay for the court appointment by calling the courthouse, explaining the situation, and asking if his appointment could be pushed back.","6":"R_5q95bC4IyTHqIgv"},"60":{"1":"Contact a reliable coworker to see if they can cover the shift until the boss arrives.","2":"Leave a detailed note for the boss or any person who might step in, explaining the situation and apologizing for the absence.","3":"Secure the store before leaving for the court appointment, making sure all goods are locked away and the cash register is secure.","4":"Inform the nearest police station about the situation, for them to periodically check the store for security.","5":"Call the boss one more time, leaving a message about the urgent nature of the court appointment and the necessity to leave the store unmanned.","